title Multi-region active/passive
direction right

Global users [icon: globe]
DNS [icon: aws-route53, description: health-checked failover]

Primary region [icon: flag, color: teal, description: us-east-1] {
  Primary edge [icon: aws-cloudfront]
  Primary LB [icon: aws-alb]
  Primary app [color: blue] {
    App A1 [icon: aws-ec2]
    App A2 [icon: aws-ec2]
  }
  Primary DB [icon: aws-aurora, shape: cylinder, description: writer]
  Primary cache [icon: aws-elasticache]
  Primary bucket [icon: aws-s3]
}
Standby region [icon: flag, color: gray, description: us-west-2] {
  Standby LB [icon: aws-alb]
  Standby app [color: gray] {
    App B1 [icon: aws-ec2]
  }
  Replica DB [icon: aws-aurora, shape: cylinder, description: reader]
  Replica bucket [icon: aws-s3]
}
Backups [icon: aws-backup]

Global users > DNS
DNS > Primary edge: active
DNS --> Standby LB: failover
Primary edge > Primary LB > App A1, App A2
App A1, App A2 > Primary DB, Primary cache
App A1, App A2 > Primary bucket
Standby LB > App B1 > Replica DB
Primary DB --> Replica DB: async replication
Primary bucket --> Replica bucket: cross-region replication
Primary DB, Replica DB --> Backups
